   "daf": "78a",
   "sentenceId": 1,
   "he": "אֲפִילּוּ הוּא עִמָּהּ בַּמִּטָּה כּוּ׳: אָמַר רָבָא: לֹא שָׁנוּ אֶלָּא בְּמִטָּה שֶׁלּוֹ, אֲבָל בְּמִטָּה שֶׁלָּהּ – מְגוֹרֶשֶׁת.",
   "en": "§ It was taught in the mishna that if he throws a bill of divorce to his wife while she is in his house, she is not divorced, «even if» the bill of divorce «is with her in the bed,» i.e., he throws it onto the bed in which she is sitting or lying. «Rava says: They taught» this «only» in a case where he throws the bill of divorce to her and it is with her «in his bed. But» if he throws the bill of divorce to her and it is with her «in her bed,» then «she is divorced.»"
  }
 ],
